  <BA_Turkic_NobleHouse.fixedName>突厥人</BA_Turkic_NobleHouse.fixedName>
  <!-- EN: Maturidism is a school of theology in Sunni Islam named after Abu Mansur al-Maturidi. It is one of the three creeds of Sunni Islam alongside Ash'arism and Atharism, and prevails in the Hanafi school of jurisprudence.\nal-Maturidi codified and systematized the theological Islamic beliefs already present among the Ḥanafite Muslim theologians of Balkh and Transoxiana under one school of systematic theology;  Abu Hanifa emphasized the use of rationality and theological rationalism regarding the interpretation of the sacred scriptures of Islam.\nMaturidism was originally circumscribed to the region of Transoxiana in Central Asia but it became the predominant theological orientation amongst the Sunnī Muslims of Persia before the Safavid conversion to Shīʿīsm in the 16th century, and the Ahl al-Ra'y (people of reason). It enjoyed a preeminent status in the Ottoman Empire and Mughal India. Outside the old Ottoman and Mughal empires, most Turkic tribes, Hui people, Central Asian, and South Asian Muslims also follow the Maturidi theology. -->
  <BA_Turkic_NobleHouse.ideoDescription>马图里迪派是逊尼派伊斯兰教中的一个神学学派，以阿布·曼苏尔·马图里迪命名。它与艾什尔里派、传统派并列为逊尼派伊斯兰教的三大教义体系，盛行于哈乃斐法学派中。\n马图里迪将巴尔赫和河中地区哈乃斐派穆斯林神学家已有的伊斯兰神学思想纳入一个系统神学学派并加以编纂和系统化；阿布·哈尼法在解读伊斯兰教神圣经典时，强调理性的运用和神学理性主义。\n马图里迪派最初局限于中亚的河中地区，但在16世纪萨法维王朝皈依什叶派之前，它已成为波斯逊尼派穆斯林的主要神学导向，也是“意见派”（重视理性者）的代表。该学派在奥斯曼帝国和莫卧儿印度享有卓越地位。在昔日的奥斯曼帝国和莫卧儿帝国之外，大多数突厥部落、回族、中亚及南亚的穆斯林也信奉马图里迪派神学。</BA_Turkic_NobleHouse.ideoDescription>
